cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Gulf-AddressBench or the tahdeed resolver, please cite it as below.
  The benchmark data are derived from OpenStreetMap (ODbL 1.0, "© OpenStreetMap contributors");
  the code is MIT. No DOI has been minted.
type: dataset
title: "Gulf-AddressBench: UAE free text address resolution with abstention, and the tahdeed resolver"
version: "2.1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-28
authors:
  - family-names: Mueen
    given-names: Huda
repository-code: "https://github.com/hudasol/tahdeed"
url: "https://github.com/hudasol/tahdeed/tree/main/bench"
license:
  - ODbL-1.0
  - MIT
abstract: >-
  A versioned benchmark for resolving free text UAE addresses (English, Arabic, Arabizi or mixed)
  to coordinates, where a system may abstain and a confident answer in the wrong place or the
  wrong city counts against it. The main sets are synthetic, rendered
  from OpenStreetMap records, and truth is the OpenStreetMap point. Two independent real text
  sets (Overture Places, Wikidata) and a 40 row hand written set are reported separately. Includes a cross city set (the same
  street or POI name in several cities, with and without the true record), a scorer with Wilson
  intervals, and baseline predictions (tahdeed, a naive fuzzy matcher, a rate limited Nominatim
  sample) whose scores are checked again in CI.
keywords:
  - geocoding
  - address resolution
  - Arabic
  - United Arab Emirates
  - calibration
  - abstention
  - benchmark
